          "enhanced_information": "In the management of a deep puncture wound from a cat bite in a 12-year-old boy, appropriate management includes Ampicillin-sulbactam administration for broad-spectrum antibiotic coverage targeting potential bacterial pathogens and surgical debridement for removal of damaged tissue and foreign material to improve wound healing. Laceration closure should be considered to seal the wound and reduce infection risk. Evidence supports the importance of removing debris and bacteria through irrigation to decrease the risk of infection."
